From: Diego <me@diegonmarcos.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 21:23:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?comms:=20fix=20About=20manual=20update=20check?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20use=20GitHub=20Releases=20API=20(fetchLatestRele?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ase/downloadApk)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0039 rewrote CommsUpdateWorker to GitHub Releases and removed the
GHCR methods (fetchToken/fetchManifestDigest/installedApkSha256/
downloadApkBlob), but FragmentOptionsCommsAbout (0036) still called them
— 4 compile errors, CI red since 0036, so the published APK never got
the 0037 Gson/R8 TypeToken fix (JMAP NoClassDefFoundError persisted).

Mirror doWork: compare rel.publishedAt vs COMMS_BUILD_TIMESTAMP
(ISO-8601 lexicographic), download rel.downloadUrl.
---
 .../eu/faircode/email/FragmentOptionsCommsAbout.java | 12 ++++++------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/FragmentOptionsCommsAbout.java b/app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/FragmentOptionsCommsAbout.java
index 51f3630897..7af9064b6a 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/FragmentOptionsCommsAbout.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/eu/faircode/email/FragmentOptionsCommsAbout.java
@@ -71,15 +71,15 @@ public class FragmentOptionsCommsAbout extends FragmentBase {
         new SimpleTask<File>() {
             @Override
             protected File onExecute(Context ctx, Bundle args) throws Throwable {
-                String token = CommsUpdateWorker.fetchToken();
-                String remoteDigest = CommsUpdateWorker.fetchManifestDigest(token);
-                String installedSha = CommsUpdateWorker.installedApkSha256(ctx);
-
-                if (installedSha != null && ("sha256:" + installedSha).equals(remoteDigest))
+                CommsUpdateWorker.ReleaseMeta rel = CommsUpdateWorker.fetchLatestRelease();
+                // Same comparison as CommsUpdateWorker.doWork: ISO-8601 sorts
+                // lexicographically; "dev" = local build, treat as up to date.
+                String installed = BuildConfig.COMMS_BUILD_TIMESTAMP;
+                if ("dev".equals(installed) || rel.publishedAt.compareTo(installed) <= 0)
                     return null; // null = up to date
 
                 File dest = new File(ctx.getCacheDir(), "updates/cloud-mail-update.apk");
-                CommsUpdateWorker.downloadApkBlob(token, remoteDigest, dest);
+                CommsUpdateWorker.downloadApk(rel.downloadUrl, dest);
                 return dest;
             }
 
